# WARP-8: on the kit a white key is the picked drum's step on every page (but Throws, the shared LFO, the master
# pages); held, the knobs lock the page's own where a step can lock them, else they are the step's trig. GLO held,
# a drum's key held on: the drum alone while it is
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
tapkey b0
# Envelope: a tap writes the step; held, knob 2 locks the page's second knob on it
tap ENV
wait 40
expect page Envelope
tapkey w0
wait 40
said step 1 on
key w4 down
wait 100
turn K2 5
wait 40
key w4 up
wait 40
expect note 1 1 5 1
expect lanes 1
# Character (FX): the same
tap FX
wait 40
tapkey w8
wait 40
said step 9 on
# Mix: a step, and held, knob 1 its velocity
tap GLO
wait 40
expect page Mix
tapkey w12
wait 40
said step 13 on
key w12 down
wait 100
turn K1 -40
wait 40
key w12 up
wait 40
expect stepvel 1 1 13 60
# a black key picks the drum here too: its step beside the kick's
tapkey b1
tapkey w12
wait 40
said step 13 on
# GLO held: a drum's key held on is the drum alone; let go, the mutes as they were
press GLO
tapkey b3
key b0 down
wait 900
expect kmute 2046
key b0 up
wait 40
expect kmute 8
release GLO
expect page Mix
